---
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
import Bare from '../../layouts/Bare.astro';
import Roadside from './_Roadside.astro';
import { STAMPS } from './_stamps';
---

<Bare
  title="Box 1725"
  description="The case file on a roadside mailbox that enforces postal law personally. Post it a stamped letter and it writes back, in words cut from the mail it has kept."
>
  <Font cssVariable="--font-box-type" slot="head" />
  <Font cssVariable="--font-box-hand" slot="head" />
  <Font cssVariable="--font-box-headline" slot="head" />

  <div class="box1725" data-box1725 data-clearance="0" data-sky="dusk" data-door-pos="shut" data-flag-pos="down">
    <section class="roadside" aria-label="The mailbox">
      <Roadside />
      <div class="tag" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="tag-line" data-status>Flag down. Nothing waiting.</p>
        <div class="tag-actions">
          <button type="button" data-write disabled>Write a letter</button>
          <button type="button" data-ledger disabled>Correspondence <span data-ledger-count></span></button>
          <button type="button" class="quiet" data-sound aria-pressed="true" disabled>Sound</button>
        </div>
        <noscript><p class="tag-line">Writing to the item needs JavaScript. The file can still be read.</p></noscript>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="folder" aria-labelledby="box1725-title">
      <a class="home" href="/">thesandbox.page</a>
      <div class="folder-tab">Item 1725</div>

      <div class="sheet first">
        <div class="clip" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="agency">Department of Irregular Mail &middot; Field Office 9</p>
        <h1 id="box1725-title">Case file: Box 1725</h1>
        <span class="stamp red stamp-irregular" aria-hidden="true">Irregular</span>

        <dl class="header-grid">
          <dt>Item</dt><dd>Curbside mailbox, Traditional pattern</dd>
          <dt>Location</dt><dd>Rural Route 9, mile <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="mile">14.6</span>, east shoulder</dd>
          <dt>Status</dt><dd>In place. <span class="ver" data-levels="0 1 2">Under observation.</span><span class="ver" data-levels="3">Observing.</span></dd>
          <dt>Disposition</dt><dd>Do not remove. <span class="tape" data-below="2" data-key="removal">Removal has been attempted three times.</span></dd>
          <dt>File opened</dt><dd>14 MAR 1988</dd>
          <dt>Last reviewed</dt><dd data-reviewed>on file</dd>
          <dt>Reviewed by</dt><dd><span class="ver" data-levels="0 1 2">Inspector <span class="tape" data-below="2" data-key="inspector">M. Okafor</span></span><span class="ver hand" data-levels="3">1725</span></dd>
        </dl>

        <fieldset class="clearance" data-clearance-switch>
          <legend>Reader clearance</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="box1725-clearance" value="0" checked /> <span>0</span> Public</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="box1725-clearance" value="1" /> <span>1</span> Carrier</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="box1725-clearance" value="2" /> <span>2</span> Inspector</label>
          <label class="locked" data-addressee
            ><input type="radio" name="box1725-clearance" value="3" disabled /> <span>3</span> Addressee <small data-addressee-note>granted by the item</small></label
          >
        </fieldset>
        <p class="aside">Redaction tape lifts if you pick at it. Lifting it is recorded.</p>
      </div>

      <section class="sheet" aria-labelledby="box1725-handling">
        <h2 id="box1725-handling"><span>1.</span> Handling</h2>
        <div class="note" data-note="ALSO. DO NOT LIE ABOUT THE FLAG."></div>
        <ol class="rules">
          <li>
            Approach only with outgoing mail. Visitors who stand at the item without posting anything report that the door
            opens on its own after about twenty seconds. <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="inside"
              >Do not look inside. It is not dark in there the way a box is dark.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            Every item posted must carry sufficient postage. Unstamped matter (circulars, menus, flyers, notes for the
            neighbors) is returned, <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="speed">at speed</span>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Do not raise the flag unless there is outgoing mail inside. The item treats a raised flag over an empty box as a
            lie, and lowers it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Do not replace the item. <span class="tape" data-below="2" data-key="replacements"
              >Replacement boxes installed in 1994, 2003, and 2011 were each recovered from inside Item 1725 within a week,
              intact, and holding mail.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>Do not strike the item. See Incident 1725-06.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="sheet" aria-labelledby="box1725-description">
        <h2 id="box1725-description"><span>2.</span> Description</h2>
        <div class="note" data-note="CORRECT. AND MISSING THE POINT."></div>
        <p>
          Item 1725 is a curbside mailbox of the Traditional pattern: a steel tunnel with an arched top, a door hinged at
          the bottom, and a red signal flag on its side, mounted on a cedar post. The pattern was drawn by a Post Office
          engineer in 1915 and left unpatented, so anyone could make it; the arched top sheds rain and snow. The item
          appears to apply the same principle to people. The name HOLLIS is stenciled on the side under two coats of
          paint.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="ver" data-levels="0">The item is ordinary in every measurable respect.</span><span
            class="ver"
            data-levels="1">The item is ordinary in every measurable respect. Carriers on Route 9 do not agree.</span
          ><span class="ver" data-levels="2 3"
            >The item is ordinary in every respect but one: its inside is larger than its outside. Measured with water in
            2004, the interior held 2.3 times the exterior volume. The measurement was not repeated. The water was not
            returned.</span
          >
        </p>
        <h3>Behavior</h3>
        <ul class="behavior">
          <li>
            It accepts only mail on which postage has been paid. That is the law (18 U.S.C. &sect; 1725); the item appears
            to regard enforcing it as its own responsibility.
          </li>
          <li>It raises its own flag when it has something for you.</li>
          <li>
            It writes back. Replies are assembled from words cut out of the mail it has kept: catalogs, circulars, seed
            packets, utility bills. No cutting instrument has been found. <span
              class="tape"
              data-below="2"
              data-key="unposted">Some words in recovered replies were cut from letters that had not yet been posted.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="sheet" aria-labelledby="box1725-incidents">
        <h2 id="box1725-incidents"><span>3.</span> Incident log</h2>
        <div class="note" data-note="I RETURNED IT. THEY PAID."></div>
        <ol class="incidents" data-incidents>
          <li>
            <b>1725-01</b> <time>11 AUG 1988</time> Carrier reports the flag raised over an empty box on 31 consecutive days
            and stops lowering it. On day 32 it lowers itself.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-03</b> <time>02 FEB 1991</time> A pizza menu left in the item without postage is found the next morning
            under the wiper of the delivery car, fourteen miles away, <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="menu"
              >folded into a small and accurate envelope</span
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-06</b> <time>19 JUL 1998</time> Item struck with a baseball bat from a moving car. The bat is returned to
            the car's registered owner by mail, postage due. <span class="tape" data-below="2" data-key="bat"
              >The postage due was paid.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-09</b> <time>06 APR 2004</time> Interior measured with water. See Description.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-11</b> <time>03 MAY 2011</time> Third replacement box recovered from inside the item, <span
              class="tape"
              data-below="2"
              data-key="third">with a seed catalog in it addressed to the item</span
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-14</b> <time>2019</time> Route 9 carrier requests reassignment. The request reads, in full: <q
              >It knows my truck.</q
            > <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="truck"
              >The carrier still drives Route 9 at 10:40 each weekday. The item raises its flag at 10:38.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>1725-17</b> <time><span class="tape" data-below="3" data-key="date">16 SEP 2026</span></time> Item begins
            replying to letters addressed to it directly. <span class="ver" data-levels="0 1">Correspondents are not
            identified.</span><span class="ver" data-levels="2 3">Every known correspondent is a reader of this file.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="sheet" aria-labelledby="box1725-exhibits">
        <h2 id="box1725-exhibits"><span>4.</span> Recovered correspondence</h2>
        <div class="exhibits">
          <figure class="exhibit envelope-exhibit">
            <div class="old-envelope">
              <span class="old-stamp" aria-hidden="true">22&cent;</span>
              <span class="hand">Occupant<br />Rural Route 9, Box 1725<br />2041</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <b>Exhibit A.</b> Envelope found in the item, stamped 1988, addressed to whoever lives here in 2041. Sealed. Left
              unopened <span class="tape" data-below="1" data-key="unopened">at the item's insistence</span>.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="exhibit">
            <div class="collage small" data-collage-static="1986" data-text="YOUR SON WILL NOT WRITE. I WILL. EVERY WEEK. POSTAGE PAID."
            >
              <p class="collage-fallback">YOUR SON WILL NOT WRITE. I WILL. EVERY WEEK. POSTAGE PAID.</p>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <b>Exhibit B.</b> Reply in cut-out words, found among the effects of <span
                class="tape"
                data-below="2"
                data-key="hollis">Mrs. A. Hollis, the item's first owner, d. 1987</span
              >. The words were cut from a hardware circular.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="exhibit">
            <div class="returned-slip">
              <p class="typed">To the item: this office requests your cooperation with an interior survey.</p>
              <span class="stamp red" aria-hidden="true">Returned &middot; Postage due</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <b>Exhibit C.</b> Memo from this office to the item, posted without a stamp. <span
                class="ver"
                data-levels="0 1 2">It was returned within the hour.</span><span class="ver" data-levels="3"
                >It was returned within the hour. So was the next one, with a stamp, because it was a request and not a
                letter.</span
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="sheet last" aria-labelledby="box1725-note">
        <h2 id="box1725-note"><span>5.</span> Reviewer's note</h2>
        <div class="note" data-note="WRITE BACK."></div>
        <p class="ver block" data-levels="0 1">
          Readers of this file may write to the item. It is not recommended. <span
            class="tape"
            data-below="2"
            data-key="recommended">It is not discouraged either.</span
          >
        </p>
        <p class="ver block" data-levels="2">
          The item does not want to be studied. It wants mail: not catalogs, letters, with postage, that expect an answer.
          It answers every one. It is easier to be near when someone has been writing to it.
        </p>
        <p class="ver block hand-note" data-levels="3">
          You have clearance now, so this part is for you. The inspector stopped writing in August. Somebody has to. Use a
          stamp.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="colophon">
        <p>
          Fiction. The Department of Irregular Mail, Route 9, the Hollis family, and Box 1725 are invented. The postal law
          is real, and so is the 1915 mailbox design.
        </p>
        <p>
          Letters you write stay in this browser and nowhere else; no letter leaves the page. Replies come from a
          hand-written grammar, not an AI. Type set in Special Elite, Reenie Beanie, and Abril Fatface (open licenses, via
          Fontsource).
        </p>
      </footer>
    </article>

    <dialog class="desk" data-desk aria-labelledby="box1725-desk-title">
      <form method="dialog" class="paper letter" data-letter-form>
        <h2 id="box1725-desk-title" class="sr">Write a letter</h2>
        <button type="button" class="stamp-slot" data-stamp-slot aria-label="Stamp: none. Pick one below.">
          <span>Place stamp here</span>
        </button>
        <label class="line to">To <input name="to" value="Box 1725, R.R. 9" maxlength="80" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        <label class="body"
          ><span class="sr">Letter</span><textarea
            name="body"
            rows="9"
            maxlength="2400"
            placeholder="Write to it. It reads everything twice."
            required></textarea></label
        >
        <label class="line from">From <input name="from" maxlength="40" autocomplete="off" placeholder="your name" /></label>
        <fieldset class="stamps">
          <legend>Stamps, one per letter</legend>
          {
            STAMPS.map((s) => (
              <button type="button" class="stamp-pick" data-stamp={s.id} aria-pressed="false" aria-label={s.label}>
                <Fragment set:html={s.svg} />
              </button>
            ))
          }
        </fieldset>
        <div class="desk-actions">
          <button value="cancel" formnovalidate class="quiet">Put it away</button>
          <button value="post" data-post>Post it</button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </dialog>

    <dialog class="reply" data-reply aria-labelledby="box1725-reply-title">
      <h2 id="box1725-reply-title" class="sr" data-reply-title>A reply</h2>
      <div class="reply-paper">
        <div class="collage" data-reply-collage></div>
        <span class="stamp red returned-stamp" data-returned-stamp hidden aria-hidden="true">Return to sender &middot; postage due</span>
      </div>
      <p class="reply-meta" data-reply-meta></p>
      <form method="dialog"><button>Fold it away</button></form>
    </dialog>

    <dialog class="ledger" data-ledger-dialog aria-labelledby="box1725-ledger-title">
      <h2 id="box1725-ledger-title">Correspondence</h2>
      <p class="aside">Kept in this browser only.</p>
      <ol class="ledger-list" data-ledger-list></ol>
      <form method="dialog" class="ledger-actions"><button>Close</button></form>
    </dialog>

    <div class="flight" data-flight aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</Bare>

<style is:global>
  body:has(.box1725) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #2a2118;
  }

  .box1725 {
    --ink: #2a2520;
    --paper: #f3ecdc;
    --paper-shade: #e6dcc3;
    --kraft: #c29b5e;
    --kraft-dark: #8f6c39;
    --red: #b3261e;
    --tape: #141210;
    --type: var(--font-box-type), 'Courier New', monospace;
    --hand: var(--font-box-hand), cursive;
    --headline: var(--font-box-headline), Georgia, serif;

    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(320px, 44vw) 1fr;
    min-height: 100dvh;
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 16px/1.6 var(--type);
  }

  .box1725 [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .box1725 .sr {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .box1725 button {
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* ---------- The roadside ---------- */

  .box1725 .roadside {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    height: 100dvh;
    overflow: clip;
    background: #0d1220;
  }

  .box1725 .scene {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .box1725 {
    --sky-0: #1b2340;
    --sky-1: #b5604a;
    --sky-2: #f0a35e;
    --sun: #ffd9a0;
    --sun-o: 0.9;
    --stars-o: 0;
    --field: #3a3324;
    --trees: #1e1a16;
    --road: #5c5550;
    --shoulder: #7d7466;
    --poles: #1d1915;
    --grass: #2e2a1c;
    --line: #d9c27a;
  }
  .box1725[data-sky='night'] {
    --sky-0: #03050c;
    --sky-1: #0e1630;
    --sky-2: #1d2747;
    --sun: #e6ecf5;
    --sun-o: 0.85;
    --stars-o: 1;
    --field: #0f1218;
    --trees: #05070a;
    --road: #1e2126;
    --shoulder: #2a2c2f;
    --poles: #07080b;
    --grass: #0c0e10;
    --line: #6e6748;
  }
  .box1725[data-sky='dawn'] {
    --sky-0: #3a4a78;
    --sky-1: #d99aa0;
    --sky-2: #f6cf9a;
    --sun: #fff1d0;
    --sun-o: 0.8;
    --field: #4b4a36;
    --trees: #2a2a24;
  }
  .box1725[data-sky='day'] {
    --sky-0: #4f86c6;
    --sky-1: #a9cbe6;
    --sky-2: #dde9ef;
    --sun: #fffbe8;
    --sun-o: 0;
    --field: #7d8a4a;
    --trees: #39452b;
    --road: #8c8681;
    --shoulder: #a69c8a;
    --poles: #3b3128;
    --grass: #5c6a32;
    --line: #f0e3a0;
  }

  .box1725 .sky-0 {
    stop-color: var(--sky-0);
  }
  .box1725 .sky-1 {
    stop-color: var(--sky-1);
  }
  .box1725 .sky-2 {
    stop-color: var(--sky-2);
  }
  .box1725 .stars {
    fill: #fff;
    opacity: var(--stars-o);
  }
  .box1725 .sun {
    fill: var(--sun);
    opacity: var(--sun-o);
  }
  .box1725 .field {
    fill: var(--field);
  }
  .box1725 .treeline {
    fill: var(--trees);
  }
  .box1725 .road {
    fill: var(--road);
  }
  .box1725 .shoulder {
    fill: var(--shoulder);
  }
  .box1725 .centerline {
    stroke: var(--line);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 14 18;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .box1725 .poles {
    fill: var(--poles);
  }
  .box1725 .wires {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--poles);
    stroke-width: 0.6;
  }
  .box1725 .grass {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--grass);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .box1725 .grain {
    stroke: #2c1d13;
    stroke-width: 0.8;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .box1725 .board {
    fill: #3d2b1e;
  }
  .box1725 .seam {
    stroke: #0b0d10;
    stroke-width: 0.8;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .box1725 .stencil {
    font: 700 13px/1 'Courier New', monospace;
    fill: #626a73;
    opacity: 0.45;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
  }
  .box1725 .latch {
    fill: #6f7780;
  }
  .box1725 .door-rim {
    fill: none;
    stroke: #555c64;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .box1725 .door {
    transform-box: view-box;
    transform-origin: 182px 318px;
    transform: scaleY(var(--door-s, 1));
    transition: transform 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.75, 0);
    cursor: pointer;
    outline: none;
  }
  .box1725[data-door-pos='ajar'] .door {
    --door-s: 0.55;
    transition: transform 3.2s cubic-bezier(0.3, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }
  .box1725[data-door-pos='open'] .door {
    --door-s: -0.34;
    transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.3, 1.1);
  }
  .box1725 .door:focus-visible .door-rim,
  .box1725 .flag:focus-visible .flag-plate {
    stroke: #ffe08a;
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .box1725 .glint {
    fill: #e8f3c4;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 1.2s;
    transform: translate(var(--gx, 0px), var(--gy, 0px));
  }
  .box1725[data-door-pos='ajar'] .glint {
    opacity: 0.85;
    transition-delay: 2.4s;
  }

  .box1725 .flag {
    transform-box: view-box;
    transform-origin: 232px 298px;
    transform: rotate(calc(var(--flag-r, 0deg) + var(--twitch, 0deg)));
    transition: transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.3, 1.6, 0.5, 1);
    cursor: pointer;
    outline: none;
  }
  .box1725[data-flag-pos='up'] .flag {
    --flag-r: -84deg;
  }
  .box1725 .flag-arm {
    fill: #9b1d17;
  }
  .box1725 .flag-plate {
    fill: #d42a20;
  }
  .box1725 .flag-pivot {
    fill: #262a30;
  }
  .box1725[data-waiting] .flag-plate {
    animation: box1725-beckon 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes box1725-beckon {
    50% {
      fill: #ff5a3c;
    }
  }

  .box1725 .tag {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    translate: -50% 0;
    width: min(92%, 420px);
    padding: 12px 14px 12px;
    background: #efe2c2;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-radius: 3px 3px 3px 3px;
    box-shadow:
      0 1px 0 #fff8 inset,
      0 8px 24px #0008;
    rotate: -1deg;
  }
  .box1725 .tag::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 14px;
    top: 50%;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    margin-top: -5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #2a2118;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #d2c09a;
  }
  .box1725 .tag-line {
    margin: 0 0 8px 34px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .box1725 .tag-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-left: 34px;
  }
  .box1725 .tag-actions button,
  .box1725 dialog form button,
  .box1725 .desk-actions button {
    padding: 6px 12px;
    font-family: var(--type);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .box1725 button.quiet {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--ink);
  }
  .box1725 .tag-actions button[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.4;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .box1725 [data-sound][aria-pressed='false'] {
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  /* ---------- The folder ---------- */

  .box1725 .folder {
    position: relative;
    padding: 56px clamp(16px, 5vw, 72px) 64px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 60% at 30% 0%, #d8b77a 0%, transparent 60%),
      repeating-linear-gradient(93deg, #0000 0 3px, #0000000a 3px 4px),
      var(--kraft);
    box-shadow: inset 12px 0 24px #0005;
  }
  .box1725 .home {
    position: absolute;
    top: 16px;
    right: clamp(16px, 5vw, 72px);
    color: #3b2a12;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .box1725 .folder-tab {
